1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,388
Rain on the window.

2
00:00:09,388 --> 00:00:24,210
A warm cup between your hands.

3
00:00:24,210 --> 00:00:34,586
Nothing is happening.

4
00:01:04,590 --> 00:02:05,429
A doorbell, seven tables, one fireplace.

5
00:02:35,430 --> 00:02:38,696
Mrs.

6
00:02:38,696 --> 00:03:31,776
Hale warms the cups first — the cup matters more than the coffee.

7
00:04:01,780 --> 00:04:59,458
The rain learns the roof, the windows fog, the same customers arrive.

8
00:05:29,460 --> 00:06:35,106
The teacher with a red pen, a Tuesday driver, and a man who loses to himself politely.

9
00:07:05,110 --> 00:07:52,757
A low fire, an old radio between stations, and a clock nobody reads.

10
00:08:22,760 --> 00:09:13,777
The lights go out — and the coffee keeps coming, by candlelight.

11
00:09:43,780 --> 00:09:55,387
I was the stranger that night.

12
00:09:55,387 --> 00:10:18,601
She lent me the umbrella and said: weather is for borrowing.

13
00:10:48,600 --> 00:10:53,616
The rain thins to drizzle; the road glitters; at midnight, Mrs.

14
00:10:53,616 --> 00:10:55,209
Hale turns the sign.

15
00:11:25,210 --> 00:11:28,057
Goodnight — the rain only learned to be quiet.
